{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLruGQzBHrGe76vkgMgw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: all four methods now raise `TypeError('Must pass only LinearEntity objects')` when either argument isn't a line, instead of crashing with `AttributeError`.\n\nThe cause was the same in `angle_between`, `smallest_angle_between`, `is_parallel` and `is_perpendicular` in `sympy/geometry/line.py`. The type check used `and` where it needed `or`, so it only raised an error when *both* arguments were invalid. Changing `and` to `or` was the whole fix: four lines, one in each method.\n\nI ran the example from the issue against all four methods and each one now raises the `TypeError`. The `sympy/geometry` test suite passes (114 passed)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":572,"cache_read_input_tokens":18958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":572},"output_tokens":229,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00a2a23a-9667-4e11-87a1-3bed4f6a8676","uuid":"3ab6ee6c-c2a8-4e7c-8e53-99c09dd07e91","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:10:04.038Z","request_id":"req_011ChLruGC6dssTnbZxh2Tq2"}
